{"skill":{"slug":"macos-calendar","displayName":"macOS Calendar"},"version":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1771354113927,"changelog":"- Added detailed usage instructions and examples to the documentation (SKILL.md).\n- Clarified JSON fields for event creation, listing all supported options and their defaults.\n- Provided best practices for parsing natural language and mapping to calendar actions.\n- Introduced critical rules for reliability, including always listing calendars first and strict input validation.\n- Explained handling of recurring events and alarm settings.\n- Improved sample commands for a wide range of scheduling scenarios.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5485,"sha256":"def5b9704ede96b884a8d034c15794515329e183849c4d5ba2263ec84a027566","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/recurrence.md","size":767,"sha256":"2c2187d429b1feaeda14f21a53ab043cdabaa81210388e2e4d24db351764b334","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/calendar.sh","size":8684,"sha256":"a954a2df2e02e07d0e694907d70a2c249348a672c101576baf29e9ee20b27509","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1921,"sha256":"52afc8273a119d51eff4fd20d6baa27159d040bf2415f90d645b0b73c9fb24dd","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789071436365,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"66d6d571a1b31662aa2d83563979db3fd0723a783dd5c831c6e1a459a1ee1ee3","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/66d6d571a1b31662aa2d83563979db3fd0723a783dd5c831c6e1a459a1ee1ee3","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: macos-calendar\nVersion: 1.2.0\n\nThe skill bundle is well-designed with strong security practices. It prevents shell and AppleScript injection by passing user-controlled JSON via stdin, performing robust validation and sanitization in Python, and passing all untrusted data as arguments to the `osascript` `on run argv` handler. The `SKILL.md` provides clear instructions without any prompt injection attempts, and the `calendar.sh` script includes logging for auditability and explicitly rejects actions on read-only calendars. No evidence of data exfiltration, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164908086},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":30,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789071436365},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill does what it says: it uses local macOS Calendar automation to list calendars and create events, with some privacy and confirmation caveats users should understand.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script runs local macOS tools, launches Calendar.app if needed, and uses Calendar.app data only; this is proportionate to the purpose but may be visible or disruptive on the user's session.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact declares macOS compatibility and required binaries for osascript and python3; no remote payload download, package install, or dependency substitution behavior was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The trigger wording covers broad reminder, deadline, and scheduling phrases, and the examples create events directly; this is purpose-aligned but users should expect real Calendar mutations when invoked.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Created calendar events and local logs persist. Logging of timestamp, command, calendar, and summary is disclosed, but event titles may contain sensitive information and the log handling is not especially hardened.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The Calendar access, AppleScript use, JSON input, recurrence support, and event creation behavior match the stated macOS Calendar purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want an agent to be able to create real Apple Calendar events on your Mac. Review ambiguous reminder or deadline requests, avoid putting highly sensitive details in event titles if local skill logs are a concern, and be aware Calendar.app may open when the helper runs.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Local execution with osascript and python3 is expected for a macOS Calendar automation skill; the metadata declares the main binaries, though it does not provide a stricter runtime permission boundary.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad reminder and scheduling triggers are aligned with the skill's purpose, but because event creation is persistent, users should review ambiguous calendar requests before allowing execution.\n[SQP-2] expected: Launching Calendar.app and creating events are expected for this workflow; the concern is lack of a script-level preview or force flag, not hidden or unrelated behavior.\n[T09] expected: The persistent action log is disclosed and local, but it stores calendar names and event summaries in plaintext and does not strongly protect against malformed log fields.\n[T09] unexpected: The documentation overstates validation: the script coerces types, only partially validates dates, and does not bound recurrence rules, which could create unintended events but does not indicate exfiltration or malicious code execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789071436365}}}}}